# $slug / $trial: quick reference

Run from the toolbox root (`$toolbox_root` at creation).

## Set the config path

```powershell
$$config = "$config_path"
```

## Preview the enabled workflows

```powershell
pixi run python scripts/run_workflows.py --config $$config --cores 3 -- --dry-run
```

## Run the enabled workflows

```powershell
pixi run python scripts/run_workflows.py --config $$config --cores 3
```

## Start a new simulation experiment

```powershell
pixi run python scripts/run_workflows.py --config $$config --cores 3 --new-experiment --note "<reason>"
```

## Preview system simulation (WF4) alone

```powershell
pixi run python scripts/simulate_system.py --config $$config --cores 3 --dry-run
```

## List runner options

```powershell
pixi run python scripts/run_workflows.py --help
```

## List simulation options

```powershell
pixi run python scripts/simulate_system.py --help
```

## Create a new trial from this one

```powershell
pixi run create-case $slug --cases-root <cases-root> --trial <name> --from-trial $trial --purpose "<purpose>"
```

## Files

| File | Role |
|---|---|
| `project_config.yml` | Project settings: data, basin, climate, enabled workflows |
$workflow_files
| `notes.md` | Trial purpose and run notes |
| `outputs/` | Results; each run reports a `summary.md` |

Docs (toolbox): `docs/guide/running.md`, `outputs.md`, `new-case.md`, `troubleshooting.md`.
